{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:21:09Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 100, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "ReportFindings", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0178wokmfcpz4AUZ2tCZgRxb", "input": {"findings": [{"file": ".gitignore", "line": 4, "category": "scope-gap", "short_summary": "backend/data/ never added to .gitignore", "summary": "The spec's own Affected Areas section requires adding backend/data/ to .gitignore, but .gitignore is unmodified in this diff, so persisted task data (potentially containing real content) has no guard against being committed.", "failure_scenario": "A developer runs the server locally, creates a few tasks (backend/data/tasks.json gets written), then runs `git add -A` / `git add backend` before a commit \u2014 the data file gets staged and committed since nothing ignores it.", "verdict": "CONFIRMED"}, {"file": "backend/app/store.py", "line": 38, "category": "correctness", "short_summary": "Non-atomic write can leave a torn/corrupt file", "summary": "_save() writes JSON directly to the live data file with Path.write_text, which is not atomic \u2014 a process kill, OOM, or power loss mid-write leaves a truncated file.", "failure_scenario": "The uvicorn process is killed (SIGKILL, host reboot, container eviction) in the middle of write_text() during a mutation. On next startup, _load() (store.py:28-31) hits a JSONDecodeError on the half-written file, catches it, and starts empty \u2014 silently discarding every previously-saved task, which is exactly the loss this feature exists to prevent. Fix: write to a temp file in the same directory and os.replace() it into place, which is atomic on the relevant platforms.", "verdict": "PLAUSIBLE"}, {"file": "backend/app/store.py", "line": 26, "category": "concurrency", "short_summary": "Silent catch-all swallows real corruption with no logging", "summary": "_load()'s bare `except Exception: return` treats a missing file and genuine data corruption identically, with zero logging, so an operator has no way to discover that saved tasks were just discarded.", "failure_scenario": "tasks.json becomes corrupted (e.g. from the torn-write scenario above, or manual edit gone wrong). Server restarts, store silently starts empty, and nothing in logs or the response indicates data was lost versus this being a fresh install \u2014 a developer only notices when their task list looks emptied.", "verdict": "PLAUSIBLE"}, {"file": "backend/app/store.py", "line": 35, "category": "concurrency", "short_summary": "Concurrent request threads can interleave writes to one file", "summary": "Route handlers in main.py are plain `def`, so FastAPI/Starlette runs each in a threadpool; nothing in TaskStore serializes _save() calls, so two concurrent mutating requests can interleave their write_text() calls into the same file. The spec's non-goal only rules out multi-process/multi-worker locking (docs/spec.md:64-66), which doesn't cover this in-process, multi-thread scenario that FastAPI's own sync-handler behavior actually creates.", "failure_scenario": "Two POST /api/tasks requests arrive close together; both handlers run in separate threadpool threads and both call _save(), and their write_text() calls interleave on the same underlying file, producing invalid JSON. On the next restart, _load() treats it as corrupt and starts empty, losing all tasks \u2014 not just the racing pair.", "verdict": "PLAUSIBLE"}]}, "session_id": "0f263f57-d158-4180-ae32-2d077689462b"}}
